WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- Love this.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.578
- Thank you.

00:00:02.578 --> 00:00:03.900
- It's so nice to meet you.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.460
I love everything you do.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.293
But I will tell you,

00:00:06.293 --> 00:00:07.920
the thing I've seen you most in is...

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:08.880
- [Kate] Oh, God.
- I'm obsessed with

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.200
Shooter. (chuckles)

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.033
- That's such a...

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:12.810
- [Kelley] I'm literally...
- Blast from the past.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:13.740
- I know, but I'm a dude.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.620
Like when it comes to films,
a lot of times, I love action.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.610
And I just had to tell you.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.723
I've literally watched
that film 39 times. Yeah.

00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:21.556
- Well it's so weird.
(audience chuckles)

00:00:21.556 --> 00:00:22.800
I shot it like a 100 years ago.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.633
- I know.

00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:24.466
- And it's on TV all the time.

00:00:24.466 --> 00:00:25.299
- And I have seen it.

00:00:25.299 --> 00:00:26.580
If you're like who's been
watching this the whole time?

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.413
- You!

00:00:27.413 --> 00:00:28.246
- It's me.
(audience chuckles)

00:00:28.246 --> 00:00:30.180
- Is it true that you
used to be really shy?

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.250
That you used to give your
mom notes and not tell her.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.650
You would just give her
notes and not talk about it?

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.000
- Yeah. I...
- This is funny.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.050
- I was so shy.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.700
I had a hard time sort of
expressing my needs or my desires.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.533
- Yeah.

00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:43.980
- And my mom was the best mom ever,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.500
used to leave me little
notes on my pillow at night

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.436
just saying, I love you.

00:00:47.436 --> 00:00:48.269
- Yeah.

00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:49.560
- Or, you know, good job today at school.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.660
And so I thought, oh
well that's a way that

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.730
I can get what I want
- [Kelley] Communicate.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.960
- without speaking to you.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.570
So I used to like slip
things in under her door

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.720
at night, you know, I really
want that Barbie or whatever.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.870
And then it became sort
of more complicated.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.480
Like when I turned I think 9,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.287
I would write I really want an agent.

00:01:09.287 --> 00:01:11.078
(Kelley and audience laughing)

00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:11.911
And she was kind of like,

00:01:11.911 --> 00:01:13.680
I have no idea how to get you an agent,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.760
but that's really cute. (chuckling)

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.600
- [Kelley] Yeah.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.800
You knew that young?

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.210
That's incredible.
- [Kate] Yeah.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.070
- Not everybody has that.
- Well, did you know young?

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:20.903
- Not at 9.

00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:22.226
- No, no, no.
- Oh. Okay.

00:01:22.226 --> 00:01:24.150
(audience chuckles)
- Like I sang, like in church.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:24.983
- Yeah.

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:25.950
Like every other human in
my community. (chuckles)

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.110
So like it wasn't special, so I didn't.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.010
No I didn't know till I was...

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.420
I don't know, like teens.
- [Kate] Yeah.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.253
- Yeah.

00:01:31.253 --> 00:01:33.277
- No, I do think it's lucky
to know at a young age.

00:01:33.277 --> 00:01:34.110
- [Kelley] Yeah.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:34.943
- Yeah, for sure.

00:01:34.943 --> 00:01:35.776
- And a lot of people
will go through their life

00:01:35.776 --> 00:01:37.470
and not, you know, they're
a jack of all trades,

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.600
but master of not one
that they really focus on,

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.433
that they love.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.790
So it's cool when they,
we find that, that young.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:42.630
- I do feel, yeah...

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.690
I feel lucky that I love it
as much today as I did then.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:46.523
You know?

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:47.399
- Yeah. Oh, that's special.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:48.232
- I know.

00:01:48.232 --> 00:01:49.065
I feel like when that goes,

00:01:49.065 --> 00:01:50.550
people always ask me like do
you think you'll ever retire?

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.260
And I'm like whenever I'm tired of it

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.580
or if it gets boring.
- [Kate] Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.630
But I still love it.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.500
- [Kate] Yeah.
- So, yeah.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.300
Yeah. Well one of your first acting jobs

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.527
was actually a Super Bowl
commercial, so that's elevated.

00:02:00.527 --> 00:02:02.700
(audience chuckling)
I was like, that's incredible.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.620
- It was really very exciting.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.870
It's still exciting today to watch it

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:10.440
because I wish I wasn't in a
Super Bowl commercial today.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.273
- [Kelley] I mean, they're huge.

00:02:11.273 --> 00:02:12.510
- [Kate] They're huge.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.343
(audience awing)
- Oh yeah.

00:02:13.343 --> 00:02:14.176
- [Kelley] Look how cute you are.

00:02:14.176 --> 00:02:15.690
- [Kate] I felt like
I was filming a movie.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.550
Like that's how exciting
it was at the time.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.870
- Well, cause it's like the first thing.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:19.703
- Yeah.

00:02:19.703 --> 00:02:21.570
- Were you more excited
about craft services?

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.403
Like, (chuckling)

00:02:22.403 --> 00:02:24.000
I always feel like every
time I talk to people,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.860
they're always like craft
services was incredible.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.500
- I brought one of our kids here today

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.150
and the thing he was most excited

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.340
about was the food that
was gonna be around.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.173
- Exactly.
- Yeah.

00:02:33.173 --> 00:02:35.070
- Check out the hallway.
There's a big hallway

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.630
full of stuff you won't want him to eat.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.130
- Yeah. (chuckling)

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.410
- So you come from a,
a huge football family.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.210
I actually did not know this about you,

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.640
but one of your parents owns the Steelers

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.170
and one owns the Giants.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.003
- [Kate] Yeah.

00:02:47.003 --> 00:02:47.970
(audience chuckling)

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.680
- And I'm gonna let that sit for a minute.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.000
Yeah. Cuz' I was like, wait, what?

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.450
And then what are football
games like at your house?

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.100
Because they get intense at my house.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:56.933
- [Kate] Yeah.

00:02:56.933 --> 00:02:57.810
- And no one owns anything.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.970
You know, we feel like we
do in spirit, but like...

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:00.803
- Yeah.

00:03:00.803 --> 00:03:02.340
- Yeah. Literally y'all own them.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.210
So like what kind of chaos
ensues out of football?

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.170
- It's pretty wild.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.390
My dad's side of my family,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.600
who are the Giants side of
the family, there's 11 kids.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.370
So my dad is one of 11.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.203
- Wow.

00:03:15.203 --> 00:03:16.830
- [Kate] So that's insane anyway.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:17.663
- Yeah.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.010
- And then they're all psycho Giant fans.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:20.843
- [Kelley] Yeah.
(audience chuckling)

00:03:20.843 --> 00:03:23.670
- So you can imagine how
crazy it is emotionally.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.830
But then I married someone who is

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.980
a psycho English football fan.
- [Kelley] Okay.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.010
- So we've got football
on the brain at all times.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.660
- Oh so you means soccer in that sense.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:34.493
Yeah. Well football.
- [Kate] Yes.

00:03:34.493 --> 00:03:35.340
But I can't call it soccer.
- Football.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.540
I know it's called football there.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.373
I just mean...

00:03:37.373 --> 00:03:39.450
So that's a lot of sports going
on in the whole household.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.283
- It's a lot.

00:03:40.283 --> 00:03:41.183
- [Kelley] Yeah.

00:03:41.183 --> 00:03:42.016
- It's a lot.

00:03:42.016 --> 00:03:43.260
- You've sung the national
anthem, so have I,

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.093
at an NFL game.

00:03:44.093 --> 00:03:46.140
So here's the thing though,
yours was pretty intense.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.040
Yours was an emotional one,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.360
cause it was a connection
to your family, right?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.193
- [Kate] Oh yeah.

00:03:49.193 --> 00:03:50.430
I think one of the last...

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.070
I don't know why I ever
sang the national anthem.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.710
I was a young, I'm not a singer.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.239
I definitely shouldn't ever...

00:03:57.239 --> 00:03:58.072
- I think you are.

00:03:58.072 --> 00:03:59.580
- [Kate] No. Like a fun,

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.770
I'll sing in the shower
or sing Disney songs.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:06.690
But my grandpa when he was
alive used to ask me to sing it.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.430
- [Kelley] Yeah.
- And so I thought, well yeah,

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.900
I should do that if he asked me.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.640
But now I just can't even.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.218
I don't know how I ever got
the guts to do it because I...

00:04:14.218 --> 00:04:15.222
- [Kelley] That's the beautiful thing.

00:04:15.222 --> 00:04:16.055
- Again, I don't feel
confident doing that.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.550
- I know, but don't you
wish you could carry that

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.110
over into like adulthood?

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.700
Like how even in the Voice,

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.890
when I have like younger
artists that I'm working with

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:25.410
they don't even know to be
jaded, or scared, or fearful.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.550
- [Kate] Yeah.
- They just go for it.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.383
- [Kate] I know.

00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:29.910
- Which is such a way that you
should live your life anyway.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.580
So I love that. I almost wish
we could carry that over.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.413
- I wish. Yeah.

00:04:33.413 --> 00:04:35.930
I wish I was as brave now
as I was then for sure.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:36.763
- [Kelley] Yeah.

00:04:36.763 --> 00:04:37.596
- Yeah.

00:04:37.596 --> 00:04:38.429
(audience clapping &amp; cheering)

00:04:38.429 --> 00:04:40.200
- The new series is called
Class of 09'. (clapping)

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.540
- Can you tell us about it? Seems intense.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.830
- Yes.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:48.830
It is a action thriller that
follows a group of FBI agents

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.490
through 3 different time
periods of their lives.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:55.470
- Yeah.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.850
- Yeah. It's very suspenseful.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.184
- Oh, I'm gonna love it.

00:04:58.184 --> 00:04:59.100
- [Kate] Oh, great.
- I love action.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:04:59.933
- [Kate] I love it.
- Love that.

00:04:59.933 --> 00:05:01.440
- [Kate] Okay good.
- I love all of that.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.550
I love stories like that.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.380
Is it good storytelling?
Like you love the writers?

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.280
The cast is pretty cool?

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.574
- The cast is so great.

00:05:06.574 --> 00:05:07.407
- Yeah.

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.910
- Brian Tyree.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:09.743
- [Kelley] Love. Yeah.

00:05:09.743 --> 00:05:11.760
- He was attached to it
before I read the script.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:12.593
There he is.

00:05:12.593 --> 00:05:13.426
- Yeah.

00:05:13.426 --> 00:05:14.259
- We just...

00:05:14.259 --> 00:05:17.100
We became a family when
we were making the show.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.030
- [Kelley] He's so talented.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.980
- He's so talented. Everyone on it.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:23.100
We really bonded intensely
over the 7 months

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.180
that we shot it.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.980
- That's fun. Well, apart from acting

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:28.410
you also have a passion
for animals, which I love.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.790
So you just posted this, so
where are you in that photo?

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.040
- [Kate] Yes. We were in Florida.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.670
I took my daughter to a
sanctuary there called

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.170
Save the Chimps.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.690
And it is such an amazing place.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.680
They have hundreds of
chimps that they've rescued

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:47.910
from different scenarios.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.360
A lot of them are from
the entertainment industry

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.310
and they... Look at how free...

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.100
I mean that's just a giant
sort of playground for them

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:56.933
and that's just one.
- [Kelley] First of all,

00:05:56.933 --> 00:05:58.890
I look at that and I'm like,
my kids would want that.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.333
- Yes. And my daughter
wanted to go play on it.

00:06:01.333 --> 00:06:03.180
- I was like, monkeys and children.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.220
- [Kate] Yes. Exactly.
- Yeah.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.060
- [Kate] But yeah it's...
- That's magical that

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.350
you get to show that kind of experience

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.700
to your daughter at like such a young age.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.533
That's cool.

00:06:09.533 --> 00:06:12.210
- I know it was her first
time seeing them in person

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.220
and she was definitely amazed.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.820
They kept doing crazy
things like, you know,

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.740
they would say hi to us
and then they'd run off,

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.083
and come back, and spit water at us.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.300
Or they'd bring a stick over

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.150
and try and get us to scratch their butts.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.050
That was a big thing.
(audience laughing)

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:28.883
- Yeah.

00:06:28.883 --> 00:06:31.055
- Can you get this for
me? Yeah. (chuckling)

00:06:31.055 --> 00:06:31.888
- Yeah. Exactly.

00:06:31.888 --> 00:06:33.660
- So I know that Dr. Jane
Goodall is a role model.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.000
So when do you think she
became a role model for you?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.230
When you were young?

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.600
- Yeah. My sister and
I, for whatever reason,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.510
when we were kids, I think it started when

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:45.330
someone gave my sister a stuffed animal

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:47.880
that looked very realistic
and it was a chimp.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.700
And we became very
obsessed with them as kids.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:54.180
And then she and I got
invited to go to Liberia

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:57.330
about 10 years ago to
visit a sanctuary there.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.163
- Yeah.

00:06:58.163 --> 00:06:59.700
- And it just changed our lives

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:04.050
and that's when I really got
to know all the amazing things

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:06.660
that Jane Goodall has done for the chimps

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.750
and just for our environment in general.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:10.740
- In general. Yeah.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.960
I agree though, I've been fortunate enough

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.970
to where I've been able to do things

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.200
and experience things like up close

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.020
and personal with just
the most majestic animals.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.870
And you're like, it does something to you,

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.660
and not makes you feel
a little in a bad way,

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.370
makes you feel so small and
like we're such a part of

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.070
something so much bigger.
And it's a beautiful thing.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.800
I think more people should
do things like that.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:32.633
- [Kate] I agree.

00:07:32.633 --> 00:07:34.000
- It's healing as well.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.281
It's very healing and it reminds you that

00:07:37.281 --> 00:07:39.390
we are all connected. You know?

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.730
That's the biggest thing
that I feel every time

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.640
I'm around them, is
that we're all the same

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.940
and so we should be treated
equally. Is is my big takeaway

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.243
every time I leave a
sanctuary of any kind.

